---
description: Fabric Loom 1.17 build conventions for Minecraft 26.x
globs: build.gradle,settings.gradle,gradle.properties
alwaysApply: false
---

# Loom 1.17 removed `modImplementation`

Mod dependencies are declared with plain `implementation`; Loom detects and remaps mods itself.
Using `modImplementation` fails configuration with "Could not find method modImplementation()".

```groovy
// ❌ BAD
modImplementation "com.geckolib:geckolib-fabric-${minecraft_version}:${geckolib_version}"

// ✅ GOOD
implementation "com.geckolib:geckolib-fabric-${minecraft_version}:${geckolib_version}"
```

## Do not add a `mappings` dependency

Minecraft 26.x has no Yarn build. Loom applies official Mojang mappings by default, so the
`dependencies` block must contain no `mappings` line at all.

## Java 25 comes from a toolchain, not a local install

Do not assume a JDK 25 is on the machine. `settings.gradle` applies
`org.gradle.toolchains.foojay-resolver-convention` so Gradle downloads it; `build.gradle` pins
`java.toolchain.languageVersion = JavaLanguageVersion.of(25)` and `options.release = 25`.

## Keep versions in `gradle.properties`

All coordinates (`minecraft_version`, `loader_version`, `loom_version`, `fabric_api_version`,
`geckolib_version`) are declared there and referenced as `${project.x}` in `build.gradle`.

## Verify versions instead of recalling them

This ecosystem moves fast and group IDs change between releases. Before adding or bumping a
dependency, check the real source rather than relying on memory or blog posts:

- Fabric loader/game versions: `https://meta.fabricmc.net/v2/versions/game`
- Fabric API and Loom: `https://maven.fabricmc.net/`
- Canonical build config: the matching branch of `FabricMC/fabric-example-mod`
- GeckoLib: its Cloudsmith maven, and the published `-sources.jar` to confirm real API signatures

Validate changes with `./gradlew build`, and confirm runtime with `./gradlew runClient` — a build
that compiles can still fail to find assets at runtime.
